Majoris Stickies for Debian 13 / Majoris OS
=======================================

Build with dpkg-buildpackage -b -us -uc on a clean Debian 13 system. The
main package does not require a Majoris ImageKit development dependency;
standard rich text and attachment file cards remain available when it is
absent. The package recipes use -Dimagekit=auto so a compatible installed
Majoris ImageKit interface provides native image previews. Majoris ISO builds
can require the dependency explicitly with:

    IMAGEKIT=enabled dpkg-buildpackage -b -us -uc

Only do so after installing the compatible ImageKit development package.

The optional extension is installed as a separate package. It is not enabled
system-wide by the package maintainer: enabling and testing the extension
must follow Majoris GNOME Shell policy for the shipped desktop version.
The extension advertises Shell 48–50 but has not been runtime-qualified.

Personal note data is stored under ~/.local/share/majoris/stickies. Debian
package installation and removal must not modify that directory.

Before an OS image release, replace the example.invalid package maintainer
address with the actual owning packaging contact and qualify binaries,
AppStream metadata, the desktop launcher, shell ABI and the save/recovery flow.

Stage 5 installs majoris-stickies-exchange for explicit single-note sharing and
app-closed synchronization through a chosen folder. The shared files are
unencrypted; do not configure a public cloud folder without user consent.
Reminders require the application to be running; no system service is installed.
